        "original_id": "85f185a2-905a-54d6-80dd-1a72023bc376",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Diana Ross\n- Places: Diana Ross Playground, The Beresford, Central Park, New York City\n- Events: Diana Ross free concerts in Central Park\n- Projects: Diana Ross Playground funding\n\nFacts:\n- On July 21 and 22, 1983, Diana Ross gave two free concerts in Central Park, and attendance was estimated at between 400,000 and 800,000 people.\n- Diana Ross pledged to fund the Diana Ross Playground project with proceeds from the television rights to those Central Park concerts.\n- Diana Ross lived across the street from Diana Ross Playground in The Beresford.\n- The Beresford is located at 211 Central Park West, between 81st and 82nd Streets, in New York City.\n- The Beresford is a luxury, 23-floor pre-war apartment building in New York City.",
